implementationPlan.description:
Prerequisite: keep the governor's temporary dependsOn 7db14e2d; before writing these overlapping paths, require the CQ-R13 supervisor/check-test checkpoint to be landed and the governor's hold lifted. Do not copy peer uncommitted overlays or wait on CQ-R13 DONE (the final hardening task needs this fix). Re-read install_dependencies and INSTALL on that checkpoint and retain its shrinkwrap/.npmrc/workspaces defenses. Establish the red regression and valid fixtures in scripts/tests/local-runner-check.test.mjs (use test-driven-development). Build on CQ-R13's current INSTALL/installRun/refusedInstall helpers: replace the fake zero-byte package manifests/locks with minimal valid, mutually matching package.json and v2/v3 lockfile-root entries, keeping KI1-KI4's existing behavioral assertions. Add table-driven pre-install refusal cases: unchanged approved lock + same-name/version file: tarball or directory in dependencies, devDependencies, optionalDependencies and peerDependencies; changed registry/npm-alias specs; added/removed dependency; mismatched peerDependenciesMeta and package name/version; overrides (direct, nested, $reference, empty and malformed); both bundleDependencies/bundledDependencies spellings. Put an invalid second directory after a valid first one and assert zero install.log entries, no relay/frame, exit 81, unchanged lock/package/source bytes and no stub node_modules bytes. Candidate script/description edits with unchanged install metadata must remain accepted. Do not edit scripts/tests/local-runner.test.mjs, which CQ-R13 owns.

Minimal matching fixture seed (new test constants are local to this file):
```js
const pkg = { name: 'fixture', version: '1.0.0', dependencies: { dep: '1.0.0' } };
const approved = { lockfileVersion: 3, packages: { '': pkg } };
// RED: write approved unchanged, but package.json dependencies.dep = 'file:../stub/dep-1.0.0.tgz'.
// Assert refusedInstall(run, label); assert.deepEqual(run.installs, []).
```
Fake-toolchain fixtures may omit non-root lock entries; real-npm tests must use valid entryOf/tarball integrity entries. Assert the unchanged lock digest and the installed stub marker's absence, not only nonzero npm status.

In scripts/local-runner/guest-supervisor.py, close the boundary in install_dependencies' existing all-directories preflight, before ANY run_install. Add one small fd-based, no-follow bounded JSON reader (reuse WALK/READ/chunks and the blob_oid traversal pattern; close every fd in finally, reject non-regular files, short/growing reads, malformed UTF-8/JSON, duplicate keys/non-JSON constants and excessive nesting). Bound package.json to 1 MiB and the lock to 16,777,216 bytes (dependency-cache.mjs MAX_LOCKFILE_BYTES); accept only object lockfileVersion 2 or 3 with an object packages['']. Treat that approved root as the authority: compare name/version when present (including presence), and exact typed dependencies/devDependencies/optionalDependencies/peerDependencies string maps plus peerDependenciesMeta; only absent versus an empty map is equivalent, never null/array/scalar or bool/number coercion. Reject overrides and both root bundled-dependency control fields whenever present because they are not approved by the lock-root contract. No semver-equivalence shortcut, spec normalization, substring ban, candidate manifest rewrite or post-install-only detection. Preserve ordinary metadata/scripts, the existing .npmrc/shrinkwrap/regular-file preflight, fixed --workspaces=false/offline/ignore-scripts argv, GUARD identity/netns/limits/timeout and no-manifest behavior. Error handling: a read, shape or comparison failure returns False through existing sanitized exit-81 handling; no candidate path or content is logged. Replace the known-hole comment with the authority rationale. Extend the same test file for size edges, malformed root/metadata/UTF-8/JSON, I/O failures, symlink/nonregular paths, valid v2/v3 and empty maps; keep all preexisting assertions.

Keep the implementation compact: reuse stdlib json.loads with duplicate-key/non-JSON-constant refusal hooks and the existing fd walk. A representative exact-map predicate is:
```py
def string_map(value):
    return type(value) is dict and all(type(k) is str and type(v) is str for k, v in value.items())

for key in ('dependencies', 'devDependencies', 'optionalDependencies', 'peerDependencies'):
    left, right = package.get(key, {}), approved_root.get(key, {})
    if not (string_map(left) and string_map(right) and left == right):
        return False
```
Here package and approved_root are new locals holding the decoded candidate and packages[''] objects. Validate name/version presence and exact string types; peerDependenciesMeta is a map of object entries and must compare with JSON type identity (True must never equal 1), including optional's boolean type. Explicit null/array/scalar is never an absent map. LockfileVersion must have exact int type, not bool/float. Catch Unicode/JSON/value/recursion/OS failures at the existing refusal boundary. Add one concise rationale comment, not a new abstraction or cross-file schema.
